{#
  PurpleForge — application-provisioning playbook for {{ lab_name }} (GENERATED,
  do not edit). Installs the third-party applications machines[].applications
  declares — today only `jenkins` is wired (see NON-AD-VULNS-ROADMAP.md
  'Application catalog' for the backlog: jira, sharepoint, wordpress, joomla,
  gitlab). Each installs a SECURE base (jenkins: security realm on, admin user,
  anonymous off, CSRF + agent-to-controller security on, confirmed answering on
  8080) — any vuln that requires_apps this host lands afterwards in
  vuln-injection, same hardening-before-gaps order as services.

  Deploy order (CLAUDE.md / site.yml.j2): runs after service-provisioning and
  before ad-population/hardening — this establishes what the machine IS (a
  running product), not a vuln or a hardening control. Application-layer sibling
  of service-provisioning.yml.
#}
---
{% for m in jenkins_hosts %}
- name: "PurpleForge | application-provisioning | jenkins -> {{ m }}"
  hosts: {{ m }}
  gather_facts: false
  tasks:
    - name: "jenkins-install | provision"
      ansible.builtin.include_tasks: "{{ '{{' }} playbook_dir {{ '}}' }}/../apps/jenkins-install.yml"
{% endfor %}
